 "stimulus_html": "In the following, calculate the payment necessary to pay off the loan with the given details. The payments are monthly.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518848,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A home improvement loan taken out for $17,950 at an annual interest rate of 7.5% for 10 years.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>To compute the payment to pay down a loan with beginning principal, <i>P</i>, the payment (<i>pmt</i>) is <span data-math=\"pmt = \\frac{{P \\times \\frac{r}{n} \\times {{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)}^{n \\times t}}}}{{{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)}^{n \\times t}} - 1}}\"></span>, where <i>r</i> is the annual interest rate (in decimal form), <i>n</i> is the number of compounding periods per year, and <i>t</i> is the number of years. Note, payment to lenders is always rounded up to the next penny.</p>\n<p>Once again, it will help you get the right answer from your calculator to find <span data-math=\"n \\times t\"></span> first.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"n \\times t = \\left( {12} \\right)\\left( {10} \\right) = 120\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"pmt = \\frac{{17,950 \\times \\frac{{0.075}}{{12}} \\times {{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.075}}{{12}}} \\right)}^{120}}}}{{{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.075}}{{12}}} \\right)}^{120}} - 1}} = \\$213.07\"></span></p>\n<p>Additional parentheses were added to help you enter the expression properly in your calculator.</p>\n<p>The payment is $213.07.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$213.07"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 518849,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A solar panel installation loan taken out for $33,760 and an annual interest rate of 4.3% for 20 years.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>To compute the payment to pay down a loan with beginning principal, <i>P</i>, the payment (<i>pmt</i>) is <span data-math=\"pmt = \\frac{{P \\times \\frac{r}{n} \\times {{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)}^{n \\times t}}}}{{{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)}^{n \\times t}} - 1}}\"></span>, where <i>r</i> is the annual interest rate (in decimal form), <i>n</i> is the number of compounding periods per year, and <i>t</i> is the number of years. Note, payment to lenders is always rounded up to the next penny.</p>\n<p>Once again, it will help you get the right answer from your calculator to find <span data-math=\"n \\times t\"></span> first.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"n \\times t = \\left( {12} \\right)\\left( {20} \\right) = 240\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"pmt = \\frac{{33,760 \\times \\frac{{0.043}}{{12}} \\times {{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.043}}{{12}}} \\right)}^{120}}}}{{{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.043}}{{12}}} \\right)}^{240}} - 1}} = \\$209.96\"></span></p>\n<p>Additional parentheses were added to help you enter the expression properly in your calculator.</p>\n<p>The payment is $209.96.</p>\n"
    },
    {
